Subject: [PATCH 06821/11362] wa30 L5 SOLVED: hand-engineered tail confirmed,
 bank +1 (72 -> 73)

The agent hit its 600-step budget cap mid-episode-3 with 5 of 6 blocks
placed and the robot 2-4 presses from the final deposit -- no live win
observed this time (weaker starting evidence than L4, which had a real
observed win). Per instruction it stopped rather than overshoot, and
handed over a candidate built from the actual 113-action episode-3
play plus a 9-action hand-engineered tail projected from determinism
evidence, explicitly flagged reproduction_verified: false and
level5_win_observed_live: false -- no overclaim.

Ran the gate on exactly that basis (genuine uncertainty, not a
rubber-stamp): extracted the 359-action full sequence and called
arc_solver_kit.reproduce(claimed_level=5) from 5 independent fresh
env.reset() calls. All 5 returned reached_level=5, reproduced=True --
the engineered tail was correct. Mechanical
arc-reproduced-count-integrity-lint passes against the updated
counters.

levels_reproduced 4 -> 5 for wa30; reproducible_total_levels 72 -> 73.

